S = {'cc': 'AG', 'fam': 'Social', 'doc': '# Antigua and Barbuda 2025: employer Social Security and Medical Benefits (2200)\n\nSources (the 1.x builder\'s copies, `world/B15-no-pit/ag/law/`): Social Security Act Cap. 408 and the Social Security\n(Collection of Contributions) Regulations (S.I. 15 of 2013, S.I. 60 of 2016) Schedule 1 row 2025: private sector\nemployee 7 %, employer 9 %, total 16 %; ceiling "$6,500.00 per month". Medical Benefits Regulations 2011 (S.I. 27 of\n2011): "An employer shall pay contributions to the Scheme at the rate of 3½% of the salary or wages" (no ceiling).\nGrade A.', 'lean': 'def ss : Contribution := Contribution.flatCapped "Social Security (employer)" 900 (6500 * 12)\ndef mb : Contribution := { name := "Medical Benefits (employer)", sched := Schedule.flat 350 }\ndef sscF : Family := employerFamily "2200 Social Security and Medical Benefits (employer)" [ss, mb] "SS (Collection of Contributions) Regs Sched. 1 (S.I. 60/2016) 2025: employer 9 % to $6,500 a month; Medical Benefits Regs 2011: employer 3.5 %"', 'families': '[sscF]', 'unsupported': [['g.household.adults.any (·.wages > 0)', 'employer Social Security 9 % (private sector) to $6,500 a month and Medical Benefits 3.5 %; public-sector rows and ages 60+ not distinguished']], 'guards': ['ss.amount 50000 == 4500', 'ss.amount 100000 == 7020', 'mb.amount 100000 == 3500'], 'taxes': [{'oecd': '2200', 'tax': 'Social Security and Medical Benefits (employer)', 'statute': 'Social Security Act Cap. 408, Collection Regs Sched. 1 (S.I. 60 of 2016); Medical Benefits Regulations 2011', 'dated': '2025 row of the S.I. 60/2016 schedule', 'grade': 'A', 'package': 'P4', 'kernel_parts': ['employerFamily', 'Contribution']}]}
